1
00:00:14,347 --> 00:00:17,183
- I'm busy!
- "Duty calls."

2
00:00:21,812 --> 00:00:24,899
"I've been trying to get you on the phone.
Open the door."

3
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:38,663
Does that board have you
any closer to catching Red John?

4
00:00:38,788 --> 00:00:40,081
I don't know.
I keep getting interrupted.

5
00:00:40,206 --> 00:00:43,417
What I need is radio silence,
Lisbon, for a week. If you can.

6
00:00:43,543 --> 00:00:45,962
The dead body at LaRoche's house
won't wait that long.

7
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:47,171
J.J.s?

8
00:00:47,296 --> 00:00:49,340
He asked for you specifically
on the case.

9
00:01:03,354 --> 00:01:04,397
Hey, boss.

10
00:01:04,522 --> 00:01:06,774
So LaRoche came home early
on a red eye from New York.

11
00:01:06,899 --> 00:01:10,486
He saw the flashlights and surprised
two robbers breaking into the safe.

12
00:01:10,611 --> 00:01:13,239
- That's when the shooting started.
- Where's the other one?

13
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:15,283
Escaped out the back.
They wore masks.

14
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:17,118
It was dark.
LaRoche didn't see much.

15
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:19,704
Oh, they hit the hummels.

16
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:22,665
- Is LaRoche okay?
- He sustained a minor hit.

17
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:24,292
Anything missing from the safe?

18
00:01:24,417 --> 00:01:26,919
Nope. He stopped them
before they could take anything.

19
00:01:27,169 --> 00:01:30,381
You know, we can have
someone handle the dog.

20
00:01:30,506 --> 00:01:31,966
Oh, yeah, I know.

21
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:36,095
- There's no I.D. on the body.
- Well, maybe not government issue

22
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:38,306
but there's a lot of information here.

23
00:01:38,889 --> 00:01:42,935
Like these black spots on his fingertips.
Dead tissue.

24
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:48,274
And his eyes are very
inflamed, too.

25
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:50,401
- Maybe he was on drugs.
- Just...

26
00:01:54,113 --> 00:01:57,491
Nice one, Lisbon.
Ibuprofen.

27
00:01:58,117 --> 00:02:01,370
I'm gonna guess this man was suffering
from rheumatoid arthritis.

28
00:02:01,662 --> 00:02:02,955
Well, if you're gonna
get in a gunfight

29
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:04,999
it's best to get in one
with an arthritic shooter.

30
00:02:06,584 --> 00:02:08,794
- Where is LaRoche?
- He's waiting in the ambulance.

31
00:02:08,919 --> 00:02:12,006
He won't let the paramedics take him
for treatment until he talks to you.

32
00:02:13,090 --> 00:02:16,010
Well, excuse me.
V.I.P.

33
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:21,140
Hey!

34
00:02:23,184 --> 00:02:24,268
J.J.

35
00:02:26,354 --> 00:02:27,688
I see you bought a new safe.

36
00:02:27,813 --> 00:02:29,315
Apparently it's not safe enough.

37
00:02:29,690 --> 00:02:32,193
- Excuse us, please.
- Yes, sir.

38
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:34,320
I'm gonna cut to the chase,
Mr. Jane.

39
00:02:34,987 --> 00:02:39,575
- I was not forthcoming with Rigsby.
- They took something.

40
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:43,412
- My Tupperware box.
- Yeah, I figured.

41
00:02:43,537 --> 00:02:46,248
Been hiding that box
for nine years.

42
00:02:46,374 --> 00:02:48,918
I thought you were the only one
that knew of its existence.

43
00:02:50,002 --> 00:02:53,214
But after the gunfire ended
the box was missing

44
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:56,384
and this was in its place.

45
00:02:56,592 --> 00:02:59,011
"Drop the case.
You have until tonight."

46
00:03:00,471 --> 00:03:01,931
What case?

47
00:03:02,723 --> 00:03:06,227
I'm investigating a security leak
inside CBI.

48
00:03:07,228 --> 00:03:11,691
The leak will turn the Tupperware
over to authorities if I don't back off.

49
00:03:12,441 --> 00:03:15,820
You know what'll happen
if they unseal that box.

50
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:20,116
- I do.
- Of course you do.

51
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:25,079
- I didn't take it.
- I know that, Patrick.

52
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:31,919
It's your favorite blackmail device.
Your puppet mastery over me ends if...

53
00:03:32,044 --> 00:03:34,338
its contents becomes public knowledge.

54
00:03:35,881 --> 00:03:37,883
I never thought of you
as a puppet.

55
00:03:38,259 --> 00:03:40,261
You ever thought of me
as a friend?

56
00:03:43,055 --> 00:03:44,974
This is difficult to ask.

57
00:03:49,228 --> 00:03:51,230
I need your help.

58
00:03:53,357 --> 00:03:57,611
- Please.
- Sure. I'll find your Tupperware.

59
00:04:00,823 --> 00:04:02,283
I would appreciate that.

60
00:04:03,617 --> 00:04:05,619
As would my mother.

61
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:10,416
You can take me now.

62
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:26,265
So what's in the Tupperware box?

63
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:32,480
I don't know.

64
00:04:46,992 --> 00:04:49,203
"Two years ago, I hired a petty thief"

65
00:04:49,536 --> 00:04:52,998
to break into LaRoche's safe
for a list of Red John suspects.

66
00:04:53,123 --> 00:04:54,666
Yeah, I know.
I had to slug the guy

67
00:04:54,792 --> 00:04:57,044
in front of his lawyer
to keep you out of jail.

68
00:04:57,211 --> 00:04:58,962
Cost me six months
in anger management.

69
00:04:59,087 --> 00:05:00,464
Yeah, and I hope
you learned something.

70
00:05:02,049 --> 00:05:05,761
My point is
he opened the safe

71
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:10,641
{\an8}- and he saw a Tupperware box.
- Which was stolen this morning.

72
00:05:10,766 --> 00:05:13,852
{\an8}To blackmail LaRoche
into dropping his investigation.

73
00:05:13,977 --> 00:05:15,103
What investigation?

74
00:05:15,229 --> 00:05:18,607
{\an8}Well, apparently there's
a security leak inside the CBI.

75
00:05:18,774 --> 00:05:19,983
Well, maybe your thief took it.

76
00:05:20,108 --> 00:05:22,861
{\an8}No, LaRoche's new safe
is way out of his league.

77
00:05:23,028 --> 00:05:28,367
{\an8}In any case, the missing plasticware
has the power to end LaRoche's career.

78
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:32,037
{\an8}- And you really don't know what's inside?
- No, I don't.

79
00:05:32,162 --> 00:05:33,622
{\an8}But LaRoche
doesn't know that.

80
00:05:33,747 --> 00:05:35,374
{\an8}So while I'm busy with him,
why don't you assign

81
00:05:35,499 --> 00:05:37,918
{\an8}Rigsby and Van Pelt
to find out what's in the box?

82
00:05:38,085 --> 00:05:40,587
{\an8}Our job is to catch
the criminal who got away

83
00:05:40,754 --> 00:05:43,590
{\an8}not protect some CBI agent
who might be dirty.

84
00:05:43,715 --> 00:05:46,134
{\an8}So much for
the anger management training.

85
00:05:49,054 --> 00:05:51,348
{\an8}If we can solve the mystery
of LaRoche's secret

86
00:05:51,473 --> 00:05:53,725
it will lead us
to the missing criminal.

87
00:05:54,351 --> 00:05:56,854
Why don't you just ask
LaRoche what's in the box?

88
00:05:56,979 --> 00:05:59,022
{\an8}He's not gonna tell me voluntarily.

89
00:05:59,147 --> 00:06:01,650
{\an8}It's embarrassing to him
and deeply personal.

90
00:06:02,442 --> 00:06:04,278
- And it's in Tupperware?
- Yes.

91
00:06:06,029 --> 00:06:08,073
{\an8}How could you not want
to investigate?

92
00:06:09,157 --> 00:06:11,285
{\an8}LaRoche told Jane he had
the box for nine years.

93
00:06:11,410 --> 00:06:13,704
{\an8}Dig into his past.
Look for significant events.

94
00:06:13,829 --> 00:06:16,748
And check out his mother. LaRoche made
a strange reference to her.

95
00:06:16,874 --> 00:06:19,710
{\an8}The Tupperware's a clue.
Why hide something in Tupperware?

96
00:06:19,835 --> 00:06:22,004
I don't know. Keep it fresh?

97
00:06:22,129 --> 00:06:23,797
Nothing stays fresh
for nine years.

98
00:06:23,922 --> 00:06:26,675
{\an8}Well, maybe LaRoche needed a box
and the Tupperware was handy.

99
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,969
{\an8}No. Tupperware's never handy.
It's always in the wrong drawer.

100
00:06:29,094 --> 00:06:30,762
{\an8}And when you do find it,
the lid's always missing.

101
00:06:30,888 --> 00:06:32,222
- Right? I hate that.
- Yeah.

102
00:06:32,347 --> 00:06:34,349
{\an8}Uh, don't let LaRoche know
you have knowledge of the box.

103
00:06:34,474 --> 00:06:36,268
{\an8}That's a confidence
between he and Jane.

104
00:06:36,393 --> 00:06:37,811
- Okay.
- We got a hit on the dead guy.

105
00:06:38,437 --> 00:06:41,398
{\an8}Will Parsons.
Local family man, married.

106
00:06:41,523 --> 00:06:43,984
{\an8}Owns a locksmith shop in El Dorado Hills.
Clean record.

107
00:06:44,109 --> 00:06:45,527
All right, let's go talk to the wife.

108
00:06:48,655 --> 00:06:52,326
{\an8}This has to be a mistake.
Will is a locksmith, not a killer. He...

109
00:06:52,451 --> 00:06:55,662
{\an8}He was on a house call,
fixing a rusted dead bolt.

110
00:06:55,787 --> 00:06:57,748
The key snapped off in the lock.

111
00:06:57,956 --> 00:07:01,960
{\an8}Your husband was part of a 2-man team
that broke into a residential home.

112
00:07:02,085 --> 00:07:04,755
{\an8}He brought his gun,
and he fired at our agent.

113
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:07,507
{\an8}If Will did that,
then somebody made him.

114
00:07:08,008 --> 00:07:11,136
{\an8}Yea... maybe they were holding
a gun on him. That's possible, right?

115
00:07:11,261 --> 00:07:13,138
When was the last time
you saw your husband, ma'am?

116
00:07:14,723 --> 00:07:17,434
{\an8}When he left the house
last night at 11:00.

117
00:07:17,601 --> 00:07:20,979
- Did you see him take his gun?
- No. No.

118
00:07:21,104 --> 00:07:23,774
Do you know anyone who might have
hired your husband to break into a safe?

119
00:07:24,274 --> 00:07:28,111
{\an8}Oh, no.
What is happening here?

120
00:07:30,781 --> 00:07:35,535
{\an8}I have suspected a security leak
inside CBI for months.

121
00:07:36,078 --> 00:07:39,623
Too many high-profile
suspects evading arrest.

122
00:07:40,123 --> 00:07:42,417
Really? Haven't noticed.

123
00:07:42,584 --> 00:07:46,213
Well, that's because you stop at nothing
to close cases for your team.

124
00:07:46,338 --> 00:07:47,464
Why, thank you.

125
00:07:47,589 --> 00:07:50,217
Other CBI agents,
they have, uh, principles.

126
00:07:51,176 --> 00:07:52,719
I leaned into that one.

127
00:07:53,428 --> 00:07:56,848
Miguel Leyva.
Sinaloa cartel.

128
00:07:57,432 --> 00:07:59,768
He controls drug corridors
throughout the East Bay.

129
00:08:00,978 --> 00:08:04,231
Two months ago, a CBI task force
was set for a bust.

130
00:08:04,398 --> 00:08:06,066
And when they raided
his warehouse

131
00:08:06,191 --> 00:08:09,277
three tons of cocaine
disappeared without a trace.

132
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:14,783
- Someone in the CBI tipped him off?
- Him and others before him.

133
00:08:14,950 --> 00:08:19,454
That was my instinct, and it was
confirmed by the arrest of this man.

134
00:08:19,663 --> 00:08:20,872
Tommy Volker.

135
00:08:20,998 --> 00:08:25,168
He was always a step ahead
of your team and I found out why.

136
00:08:25,627 --> 00:08:28,338
He had a secret
cell phone account.

137
00:08:28,463 --> 00:08:32,676
Now, in the days before his arrest
that number was called six times...

138
00:08:33,427 --> 00:08:35,095
from inside CBI.

139
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:39,516
- Well, at least you have a suspect.
- Of which I am not aware.

140
00:08:40,225 --> 00:08:42,102
The thief who got away.

141
00:08:43,270 --> 00:08:47,065
Huh? You find the thief
you find the leak.

142
00:08:47,816 --> 00:08:52,070
Before tonight. That's when my blackmailer
will expose the truth about me.

143
00:08:52,195 --> 00:08:54,114
Well, like you said,
I'll stop at nothing.

144
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:58,660
You know what's
in that box, Patrick.

145
00:09:01,204 --> 00:09:05,042
- What do you think of me?
- You...

146
00:09:05,625 --> 00:09:08,295
You're gonna have to be
a little more, uh, specific.

147
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:11,923
Am I a monstrosity to you?

148
00:09:12,716 --> 00:09:14,384
A monstrosity?

149
00:09:15,594 --> 00:09:18,221
No.
I mean...

150
00:09:19,598 --> 00:09:23,143
You're... you're interesting
and you're complex.

151
00:09:23,435 --> 00:09:26,730
- I am?
- And obviously creative. Tupperware...

152
00:09:28,398 --> 00:09:31,151
Well, I suppose
that's true.

153
00:09:33,779 --> 00:09:35,989
I've been afraid to ask that
until now.

154
00:09:38,992 --> 00:09:40,160
Excuse me.

155
00:09:45,082 --> 00:09:46,416
Found something.

156
00:09:46,541 --> 00:09:50,087
Nine years ago, LaRoche's mother
was physically and sexually assaulted.

157
00:09:50,754 --> 00:09:52,714
The attack lasted two hours.

158
00:09:53,131 --> 00:09:54,925
She said she begged
for mercy the whole time

159
00:09:55,050 --> 00:09:59,304
- but... her rapist just ignored her.
- Wow. Did she survive?

160
00:09:59,429 --> 00:10:01,223
Three months later,
she took her life.

161
00:10:01,431 --> 00:10:03,683
Oh... poor LaRoche.

162
00:10:04,643 --> 00:10:07,104
What does all this have to do
with a plastic container?

163
00:10:07,479 --> 00:10:09,147
What if there was evidence inside?

164
00:10:10,273 --> 00:10:13,568
Scott Saynay. The man convicted
of raping LaRoche's mother.

165
00:10:14,194 --> 00:10:16,363
He's serving a 12-year
sentence in Folsom.

166
00:10:17,155 --> 00:10:19,741
What if LaRoche planted
evidence to assure his conviction?

167
00:10:20,117 --> 00:10:23,620
- Like what?
- I don't know. His mother's blood?

168
00:10:23,787 --> 00:10:26,331
I mean, it says here that
the only physical evidence

169
00:10:26,456 --> 00:10:29,042
linking Saynay to the crime
is her blood on his clothes.

170
00:10:29,167 --> 00:10:31,253
Why would LaRoche
want to keep that?

171
00:10:31,837 --> 00:10:35,340
Maybe he thought he'd need it again
if Saynay got out on appeal.

172
00:10:35,507 --> 00:10:36,925
Oh... this is crazy.

173
00:10:37,050 --> 00:10:39,177
How can the boss possibly
expect us to solve this?

174
00:10:39,302 --> 00:10:40,762
I don't know, but I really want
to know what's in that box.

175
00:10:40,887 --> 00:10:42,764
Yeah, me, too.
I wonder if he knows.

176
00:10:46,226 --> 00:10:49,062
Hi. Can I get
a medium coffee, please?

177
00:10:50,438 --> 00:10:52,816
- Lisbon. I was looking for you.
- Hey, Brenda.

178
00:10:52,941 --> 00:10:54,818
Any developments
on the LaRoche break-in?

179
00:10:54,943 --> 00:10:57,028
Not yet, no. Why?

180
00:10:57,279 --> 00:10:59,990
The head of our Internal Affairs division
was shot inside his home this morning.

181
00:11:00,115 --> 00:11:01,533
We need to get out
in front of the case.

182
00:11:01,658 --> 00:11:04,244
Well, that's what I'm trying to do.
I'm heading to the autopsy now.

183
00:11:04,369 --> 00:11:06,163
I mean from a public perspective.

184
00:11:06,288 --> 00:11:09,332
We can't allow people to believe
there's corruption brewing inside CBI.

185
00:11:09,541 --> 00:11:11,084
Is that what people believe?

186
00:11:11,209 --> 00:11:13,628
There's been some chatter
in the local blogosphere.

187
00:11:13,753 --> 00:11:16,339
- I don't read blogs.
- Well, you should.

188
00:11:16,798 --> 00:11:18,675
It's easy to forget, but we work
in the state capital.

189
00:11:18,842 --> 00:11:20,594
Now I just came
from Bertram's office.

190
00:11:20,719 --> 00:11:22,345
He agrees with me
that a TV interview

191
00:11:22,470 --> 00:11:25,056
with a friendly reporter
is a win-win for the Bureau.

192
00:11:25,182 --> 00:11:27,851
- Well, let's win.
- I'll get back to you with details.

193
00:11:30,604 --> 00:11:32,272
No obstruction of the airway.

194
00:11:33,899 --> 00:11:38,612
The mucosa of the epiglottis, glottis,
and major bronchi are anatomic.

195
00:11:40,947 --> 00:11:42,490
Thanks for coming by.

196
00:11:42,616 --> 00:11:44,451
Since when do we attend autopsies?

197
00:11:44,576 --> 00:11:48,288
Well, since we have a deadline to confirm
my diagnosis at the crime scene.

198
00:11:48,997 --> 00:11:51,791
No injuries to the respiratory
system that I can see.

199
00:11:51,958 --> 00:11:53,919
Rheumatoid arthritis, right?
And?

200
00:11:54,044 --> 00:11:58,506
Well, this man... was at war with his body,
Lisbon, specifically his hands.

201
00:11:58,632 --> 00:12:00,884
Um, would you explain, Doc?

202
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:04,429
See the swelling and inflammation
around the wrists?

203
00:12:04,596 --> 00:12:07,098
It created a compression
of the medial nerve inside.

204
00:12:07,224 --> 00:12:08,600
Carpal tunnel, basically.

205
00:12:08,808 --> 00:12:11,895
Any repetitive use of the subject's hands
would have caused great pain.

206
00:12:12,729 --> 00:12:15,315
- A locksmith who can't use his hands?
- There's more.

207
00:12:15,482 --> 00:12:17,692
I noticed thickening and scarring
of the pericardium...

208
00:12:17,817 --> 00:12:19,903
that's the sac-like structure
around the heart.

209
00:12:20,070 --> 00:12:22,322
- You can see it here.
- I'll take your word for it.

210
00:12:23,031 --> 00:12:26,201
Chronic chest pain and shortness of breath
were a way of life for this man.

211
00:12:27,077 --> 00:12:28,245
Thanks, Doc.

212
00:12:29,371 --> 00:12:32,791
I don't get it. Why would somebody hire
a disabled thief to rob a safe?

213
00:12:32,958 --> 00:12:34,251
Well, you wouldn't.
Not knowingly.

214
00:12:34,376 --> 00:12:36,586
Now you said Parsons here
owned a locksmith business?

215
00:12:36,711 --> 00:12:38,630
- Yeah, with his wife.
- I'd like to meet her.

216
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:49,432
Mom's been a wreck
since your visit this morning.

217
00:12:49,641 --> 00:12:51,393
She's taking the news
really hard.

218
00:12:51,643 --> 00:12:55,897
- She and my dad were crazy close.
- Oh, we'll try to keep this brief.

219
00:12:57,315 --> 00:13:01,444
Mom? The CBI agents want to ask you
a few more questions.

220
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:05,031
Okay, fine.

221
00:13:05,907 --> 00:13:08,034
Jenna, this is Patrick Jane.

222
00:13:08,493 --> 00:13:11,454
- Hi. I'm sorry for your loss.
- Thank you.

223
00:13:12,414 --> 00:13:14,749
Sarah, could you please
make us some tea?

224
00:13:16,626 --> 00:13:17,669
Please.

225
00:13:20,088 --> 00:13:23,216
I told Sarah her father had been shot
but I didn't mention the robbery.

226
00:13:23,341 --> 00:13:25,302
I'm counting on you
to straighten that out.

227
00:13:25,427 --> 00:13:27,053
Oh, we're working on it.

228
00:13:28,138 --> 00:13:30,223
Quite a safe collection
your husband had.

229
00:13:31,558 --> 00:13:32,851
Well, he had more.

230
00:13:33,435 --> 00:13:35,895
But we had to sell some off
when the economy took a dive.

231
00:13:36,062 --> 00:13:37,105
Yeah.

232
00:13:37,230 --> 00:13:38,898
Yeah, well, most people
collect for sentimental reasons.

233
00:13:39,024 --> 00:13:41,776
It's an attempt to trigger
a fond memory.

234
00:13:41,901 --> 00:13:43,820
I'm gonna guess... I'm gonna
go out on a limb here

235
00:13:44,029 --> 00:13:46,865
and guess that your husband's collection
started with this little fella.

236
00:13:47,157 --> 00:13:49,034
Will found that when he was 7.

237
00:13:49,868 --> 00:13:51,953
It was locked, so he was dying
to know what was inside

238
00:13:52,078 --> 00:13:54,789
and he spent months trying every
possible number combination

239
00:13:54,914 --> 00:13:58,335
until finally one misty
morning, it opened.

240
00:13:58,460 --> 00:14:01,588
- What was inside?
- I don't remember.

241
00:14:02,422 --> 00:14:03,673
That's a disappointment.

242
00:14:03,798 --> 00:14:06,009
No, Lisbon, it doesn't matter
what was inside.

243
00:14:06,509 --> 00:14:08,887
The exciting part is
the mystery of not knowing.

244
00:14:09,012 --> 00:14:10,972
It's what makes
the journey memorable.

245
00:14:11,097 --> 00:14:13,433
Will spent his entire career
following that journey.

246
00:14:13,558 --> 00:14:16,019
It's what made him become a locksmith.

247
00:14:16,811 --> 00:14:21,107
Jenna, we found out that he was
losing the use of his hands.

248
00:14:21,232 --> 00:14:23,401
Why didn't you tell us
about that earlier?

249
00:14:23,568 --> 00:14:25,195
I didn't think of it.
You'd just told me

250
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:27,947
the man I spent
my entire life with was dead.

251
00:14:28,239 --> 00:14:30,283
Which I still don't understand.

252
00:14:30,450 --> 00:14:33,495
The first step is finding out
who he broke into that house with.

253
00:14:33,661 --> 00:14:36,414
- Did he have any employees?
- No. It was just Will.

254
00:14:36,873 --> 00:14:38,750
He wanted to hire
a good locksmith

255
00:14:38,875 --> 00:14:42,295
to cut down on his workload, but he couldn't
find anybody up to his standards.

256
00:14:43,171 --> 00:14:47,050
- That's incredibly valuable.
- You know about safes?

257
00:14:47,592 --> 00:14:52,222
- Do you have the combination for this?
- No. Will kept those in his head.

258
00:14:53,681 --> 00:14:55,475
I was hoping you'd say that.

259
00:14:57,352 --> 00:15:01,356
- Wait! What're you doing? What?
- Jane! Stop it!

260
00:15:01,689 --> 00:15:03,525
Mom! What's he doing?

261
00:15:03,650 --> 00:15:05,735
What are you, crazy?
That's airtight!

262
00:15:05,902 --> 00:15:07,445
Then you'd better
get to work then.

263
00:15:07,612 --> 00:15:10,657
Mom! We have to do something.
What do we do?

264
00:15:12,325 --> 00:15:13,701
I've got it.

265
00:15:25,463 --> 00:15:27,090
How's she know
how to do that?

266
00:15:27,424 --> 00:15:29,634
Your father was losing
the use of his hands.

267
00:15:29,801 --> 00:15:31,678
He needed help, so he taught
everything he knew

268
00:15:31,803 --> 00:15:33,555
to the woman he trusted most.

269
00:15:33,888 --> 00:15:35,056
How come
I don't know this?

270
00:15:35,181 --> 00:15:37,725
Well, I imagine your father
was a proud man, too.

271
00:15:38,935 --> 00:15:42,480
Too proud to let anyone know
his wife was doing his job for him.

272
00:15:44,941 --> 00:15:46,276
Et voila!

273
00:15:49,195 --> 00:15:51,406
Okay, take it.

274
00:15:52,991 --> 00:15:54,784
You're gonna have to come
with us now.

275
00:15:55,034 --> 00:15:56,786
Turn around.
Put your hands behind your back.

276
00:15:56,953 --> 00:15:59,289
What, you're arresting her?
For what?

277
00:15:59,456 --> 00:16:01,749
Breaking and entering,
safecracking, and armed robbery.

278
00:16:01,875 --> 00:16:03,209
That sound about right?

279
00:16:15,052 --> 00:16:17,513
I'm the one who opened
your agent's safe.

280
00:16:17,889 --> 00:16:20,808
It was a Sargent and Greenleaf lock
and they can take hours

281
00:16:20,933 --> 00:16:24,395
and Will, just...
moving his fingers hurt so much.

282
00:16:24,979 --> 00:16:27,732
And who hired you to break
into Agent LaRoche's home?

283
00:16:28,691 --> 00:16:30,276
Will never said.

284
00:16:30,443 --> 00:16:33,112
He just said somebody called
and offered him a lot of money

285
00:16:33,237 --> 00:16:35,156
to open a residential safe.

286
00:16:36,365 --> 00:16:40,036
- What were you asked to steal?
- A plastic container.

287
00:16:40,745 --> 00:16:43,289
I don't know what was in it.
I didn't ask.

288
00:16:44,790 --> 00:16:46,167
Where is it, ma'am?

289
00:16:47,335 --> 00:16:50,505
- Where's the plastic container you stole?
- We, um...

290
00:16:52,423 --> 00:16:57,053
We had a drop point.
A storm drain in Woodley Park.

291
00:16:57,845 --> 00:16:59,847
When you left the shop
this morning, I...

292
00:17:00,139 --> 00:17:02,308
drove to the park
and left the container.

293
00:17:03,601 --> 00:17:08,439
- And you never looked inside?
- No. I just wanted it to be done with.

294
00:17:08,606 --> 00:17:11,275
"My husband lost his life
over that stupid box."

295
00:17:12,026 --> 00:17:15,863
- You think we're too late?
- Never know unless you try.

296
00:17:25,164 --> 00:17:27,792
Did your contact say
where the storm drain was?

297
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,086
Near a warning sign.

298
00:17:53,150 --> 00:17:54,652
Someone's already been here.

299
00:18:04,203 --> 00:18:05,413
There.

300
00:18:09,750 --> 00:18:11,669
- CBI! Down on the ground!
- Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

301
00:18:11,794 --> 00:18:13,087
Put your hands
where I can see them! Down!

302
00:18:13,212 --> 00:18:16,048
- What'd I do?
- Now! On your knees! Get down now!

303
00:18:16,173 --> 00:18:18,676
He's usually a very calm man.
Now do as he says.

304
00:18:18,884 --> 00:18:21,637
- Okay. Just don't shoot.
- Secure the container, please.

305
00:18:30,938 --> 00:18:32,732
Should probably check it
to be sure.

306
00:18:41,741 --> 00:18:42,950
- Daddy?
- It's okay, buddy.

307
00:18:43,075 --> 00:18:44,577
Everything's gonna be all right.

308
00:18:47,330 --> 00:18:48,914
Banana and peanut butter.

309
00:18:55,838 --> 00:18:58,257
You're a lucky kid.
Looks tasty.

310
00:18:59,634 --> 00:19:03,095
I am very sorry, sir.

311
00:19:05,264 --> 00:19:06,307
Have a nice day.

312
00:19:06,432 --> 00:19:08,100
Come on, buddy.
Let's get out of here.

313
00:19:15,191 --> 00:19:16,817
My time is running out.

314
00:19:17,902 --> 00:19:21,030
Whatever happens, I want
to thank you for trying to help me.

315
00:19:21,405 --> 00:19:24,575
Well, truth is, you're
a hard man not to help, LaRoche.

316
00:19:24,909 --> 00:19:28,120
You're like a Shar-Pei puppy
that's rolled onto its back.

317
00:19:28,454 --> 00:19:31,207
- You have to rub its belly.
- You're mocking me.

318
00:19:31,332 --> 00:19:33,876
No, no, I'm happy
to rub your belly.

319
00:19:34,210 --> 00:19:36,671
- That won't be necessary.
- I hope not.

320
00:19:43,094 --> 00:19:44,595
Should be here somewhere.

321
00:19:44,804 --> 00:19:47,056
- Uh, what was the name again?
- Scott Saynay.

322
00:19:47,181 --> 00:19:49,892
He's serving a 12-year sentence
for rape and indecent assault.

323
00:19:50,059 --> 00:19:55,439
Oh, here it is. Scott Saynay was here.
Early release. Six weeks ago.

324
00:19:55,648 --> 00:20:01,404
- Oh. Where's he now?
- Should be in here somewhere.

325
00:20:01,570 --> 00:20:03,614
Sorry for the mess,
but the Supreme Court just ruled

326
00:20:03,739 --> 00:20:06,742
that prison overcrowding
is unconstitutional.

327
00:20:06,867 --> 00:20:08,786
- What a bother.
- I know, right?

328
00:20:08,911 --> 00:20:11,831
We have to reduce our numbers
by 1,800 this year.

329
00:20:12,164 --> 00:20:14,917
Saynay was one of
the lucky ones.

330
00:20:17,878 --> 00:20:21,257
Looks like the release file
was forwarded.

331
00:20:21,966 --> 00:20:23,843
You could find him
through his parole officer.

332
00:20:23,968 --> 00:20:27,638
- And who would that be?
- It's in the release file.

333
00:20:28,013 --> 00:20:30,808
But I could put a trace on it.
Might take a few days.

334
00:20:30,933 --> 00:20:32,435
Yeah, we don't have a few days.

335
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:34,729
Uh, maybe we could talk
to Saynay's last cellmate.

336
00:20:34,854 --> 00:20:39,191
Oh! That's a good idea.
Let's see who that was.

337
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:41,777
Yes. Ahh...

338
00:20:42,111 --> 00:20:45,698
Okay, should be in here
somewhere.

339
00:20:52,371 --> 00:20:55,207
According to the records, you were
Scott Saynay's last roommate?

340
00:20:55,332 --> 00:20:58,085
Saynay? Y-yeah, sure,
I remember him.

341
00:20:58,461 --> 00:21:00,421
Easiest cellie I ever had.

342
00:21:00,546 --> 00:21:02,965
Spent most nights writing
letters to his ma.

343
00:21:03,215 --> 00:21:06,886
Did Saynay ever give you a sense
that he felt wrongly accused or set up?

344
00:21:07,762 --> 00:21:12,141
Nah. He wasn't fighting any drama.
Not that you'd know it if he was.

345
00:21:12,558 --> 00:21:16,604
- My boy wasn't much of a talker.
- What's so funny?

346
00:21:17,104 --> 00:21:20,566
Ah, you'd have to meet Saynay
to fully appreciate his quiet nature.

347
00:21:21,317 --> 00:21:24,111
Did he ever mention
a plastic container to you?

348
00:21:24,278 --> 00:21:27,782
- What plastic container?
- I guess he didn't trust him enough.

349
00:21:27,948 --> 00:21:30,075
- No, clearly.
- What are you talking about?

350
00:21:30,367 --> 00:21:33,245
We're trying to locate
an airtight plastic box.

351
00:21:33,370 --> 00:21:34,789
Your cellmate knew all about it.

352
00:21:34,914 --> 00:21:36,290
It was hidden in a safe for nine years

353
00:21:36,415 --> 00:21:38,501
but a man was killed
stealing it this morning.

354
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:41,420
Well, I'll be damned.

355
00:21:41,796 --> 00:21:43,547
Wait. You know
what's in the box?

356
00:21:43,714 --> 00:21:45,591
Well, I can guess.
Can't you?

357
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:48,886
- Oh, we want to hear your guess.
- Nothing in that for me

358
00:21:49,053 --> 00:21:50,596
except I'd be pissing off
the owner of the box

359
00:21:50,721 --> 00:21:53,057
and who wants to mess
with a maniac like that?

360
00:21:53,724 --> 00:21:55,601
I'm done answering
their questions.

361
00:21:56,811 --> 00:21:58,813
Scott Saynay, convicted
nine years ago

362
00:21:58,938 --> 00:22:00,523
of raping and beating
LaRoche's mother.

363
00:22:00,648 --> 00:22:02,483
She committed suicide
three months later.

364
00:22:02,691 --> 00:22:05,736
That certainly qualifies
as a dramatic event in his life.

365
00:22:05,861 --> 00:22:07,905
He just got out of prison.
We're trying to track him down.

366
00:22:08,656 --> 00:22:10,908
Other than being an extreme
form of lowlife

367
00:22:11,033 --> 00:22:12,326
what else did you learn
about him?

368
00:22:12,493 --> 00:22:14,703
All we have are his arrest files
but there's nothing surprising.

369
00:22:14,870 --> 00:22:16,789
He's a high school dropout,
unemployed.

370
00:22:16,914 --> 00:22:18,290
Multiple burglary arrests.

371
00:22:18,457 --> 00:22:21,377
He was on antidepressants the night
he attacked Mrs. LaRoche.

372
00:22:21,502 --> 00:22:24,421
Then maybe he hired the locksmith
to open LaRoche's safe.

373
00:22:24,588 --> 00:22:27,967
No. The break-in is connected
to LaRoche's internal investigation.

374
00:22:28,092 --> 00:22:29,593
That, I'm certain of.

375
00:22:29,718 --> 00:22:32,263
So we still don't know
what's in the box or who has it?

376
00:22:32,388 --> 00:22:34,765
Okay, Teresa. Reporter's
here for your interview.

377
00:22:34,890 --> 00:22:37,017
Ah, Sacramento's most
eligible singles

378
00:22:37,184 --> 00:22:41,313
or should I say,
sexy spinsters of Sacramento?

379
00:22:41,689 --> 00:22:44,984
Bertram wants to put a public
face on the LaRoche break-in.

380
00:22:45,109 --> 00:22:46,151
Why?

381
00:22:46,277 --> 00:22:49,363
To assure the public that we are not
rattled by criminal attacks on our people.

382
00:22:49,530 --> 00:22:52,032
But LaRoche was rattled.
He was shot.

383
00:22:52,199 --> 00:22:55,369
Just... let me do what I do.
You do what you do.

384
00:22:55,536 --> 00:22:57,413
Whatever that is.
Lisbon, this way, please.

385
00:22:59,915 --> 00:23:02,251
You only have 15 minutes.
Let's get this thing going.

386
00:23:02,376 --> 00:23:03,669
You're the boss, Brenda.

387
00:23:03,919 --> 00:23:06,255
- Really?
- Ah, I just let her think so.

388
00:23:06,380 --> 00:23:08,090
We haven't officially met.
Mason Braverman.

389
00:23:08,215 --> 00:23:09,967
Teresa Lisbon.
I have anything in my teeth?

390
00:23:10,134 --> 00:23:12,720
- No, you're good. You're good.
- Okay, good. Let's do it.

391
00:23:13,304 --> 00:23:14,972
This is the second time

392
00:23:15,097 --> 00:23:17,433
Agent LaRoche's home
has been broken into, isn't it?

393
00:23:17,558 --> 00:23:18,934
"Yes, it is."

394
00:23:19,768 --> 00:23:21,437
What's he hiding in there?
Jimmy Hoffa?

395
00:23:21,562 --> 00:23:24,690
Uh, we don't know why
Agent LaRoche's home was targeted.

396
00:23:24,815 --> 00:23:26,901
He killed one of the robbers
in a gunfight.

397
00:23:27,026 --> 00:23:28,444
We have the other one in custody

398
00:23:28,569 --> 00:23:30,905
and we expect to have
some information soon.

399
00:23:31,113 --> 00:23:32,281
You're certainly having more luck

400
00:23:32,406 --> 00:23:34,992
than the CBI task force that
botched the Miguel Leyva raid.

401
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:39,163
We heard the dangerous cartel boss is free
because someone tipped him off.

402
00:23:39,288 --> 00:23:41,874
- "That's not my case."
- Okay. Turn off the camera.

403
00:23:41,999 --> 00:23:43,876
We agreed to a line
of questioning, Mason.

404
00:23:44,043 --> 00:23:45,085
Uh, no.

405
00:23:45,210 --> 00:23:46,253
- In exchange, I promised you...
- A line of questioning...

406
00:23:46,378 --> 00:23:47,421
- access and an exclusive story.
- Which I never agreed to, Brenda.

407
00:23:47,546 --> 00:23:49,632
Why don't I just step out
while you two clear this up?

408
00:23:49,757 --> 00:23:52,509
Teresa, be patient.
I can always call Channel 10.

409
00:23:52,635 --> 00:23:56,180
- It's your choice.
- No, I'm good.

410
00:24:02,937 --> 00:24:06,190
So, how does this home invasion
affect other CBI agents?

411
00:24:06,315 --> 00:24:08,484
The targeting
of Agent LaRoche's home...

412
00:24:08,651 --> 00:24:11,487
is stark evidence that
no law enforcement officer

413
00:24:11,612 --> 00:24:14,531
"is ever truly off duty.
We're all targets."

414
00:24:15,115 --> 00:24:18,243
"But J.J. LaRoche chose
to be a CBI agent"

415
00:24:18,369 --> 00:24:20,829
"which is a life
of serving other people."

416
00:24:21,163 --> 00:24:23,666
"We all know the game,
and we all accept the risks."

417
00:24:47,104 --> 00:24:48,271
Heard you had some
news on the case.

418
00:24:48,397 --> 00:24:50,565
The phone company just confirmed
that a call was made

419
00:24:50,691 --> 00:24:52,859
from the CBI
to the locksmith's shop.

420
00:24:52,985 --> 00:24:54,903
LaRoche is right.
We've got an internal leak.

421
00:24:55,070 --> 00:24:58,490
That's not news, Lisbon.
A phone extension would be news.

422
00:24:58,657 --> 00:25:00,742
Well, they could only trace it
to the general switchboard.

423
00:25:00,909 --> 00:25:04,037
We're still walking around blind, Lisbon.
And we're pressed for time.

424
00:25:04,204 --> 00:25:06,832
LaRoche is pressed for time.
We're doing fine.

425
00:25:06,999 --> 00:25:09,501
Hey, boss.
I might have a lead.

426
00:25:10,502 --> 00:25:12,212
I found this newspaper
story in the archives.

427
00:25:12,337 --> 00:25:13,755
It ran seven years ago.

428
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:15,674
"Will Parsons likes to play safe"?

429
00:25:15,966 --> 00:25:17,968
It's a local profile
on Parsons and his collection.

430
00:25:18,135 --> 00:25:21,471
Same year, he entered a national
safecracking competition. Placed seventh.

431
00:25:21,596 --> 00:25:24,099
So you're thinking
that the CBI leak read this article

432
00:25:24,224 --> 00:25:25,726
and knew that Parsons
could do the job?

433
00:25:25,851 --> 00:25:26,893
It's a safe bet.

434
00:25:29,438 --> 00:25:31,857
- That's funny.
- What is?

435
00:25:33,775 --> 00:25:35,068
Never mind.

436
00:25:35,318 --> 00:25:37,446
All right, see who else
is logged into the archive

437
00:25:37,571 --> 00:25:41,533
and see if any CBI personnel are long-time
subscribers to the "Weekly."

438
00:25:41,658 --> 00:25:44,369
Uh, I just may have
saved you the trouble.

439
00:25:44,703 --> 00:25:47,205
Uh... look at the masthead.

440
00:25:47,873 --> 00:25:50,375
Specifically, look who
the managing editor was

441
00:25:50,500 --> 00:25:52,544
at the "Sacramento Weekly"
seven years ago.

442
00:25:53,003 --> 00:25:54,838
Brenda Shettrick?

443
00:25:55,005 --> 00:25:57,883
- No way. Brenda?
- Makes sense.

444
00:25:58,508 --> 00:26:01,553
Most information inside CBI
runs through Shettrick.

445
00:26:02,429 --> 00:26:05,474
With time, I can build a case, but...

446
00:26:05,766 --> 00:26:08,268
- time is passing quickly.
- We always have time.

447
00:26:08,393 --> 00:26:09,978
You know how long it takes me
to solve a case?

448
00:26:10,937 --> 00:26:13,190
However long I have.

449
00:26:13,398 --> 00:26:19,321
But in certain situations,
when I'm in a true pinch, such as this

450
00:26:19,946 --> 00:26:22,199
there are compromises
that need to be made.

451
00:26:22,449 --> 00:26:23,617
What kind of compromises?

452
00:26:23,784 --> 00:26:27,454
Well, for instance, I could... I could
bring down Shettrick before tonight

453
00:26:27,621 --> 00:26:29,831
but I will have to enlist the help
of Lisbon and the team.

454
00:26:29,956 --> 00:26:36,338
No. Nobody can know
about the plastic box

455
00:26:36,463 --> 00:26:38,548
or that it was taken
from my safe.

456
00:26:40,133 --> 00:26:41,927
They already know.

457
00:26:43,220 --> 00:26:45,472
I had to confide in Lisbon

458
00:26:45,847 --> 00:26:48,141
that a very valuable box
was stolen from you

459
00:26:48,266 --> 00:26:51,186
but I did not tell her
what was inside, I swear.

460
00:26:52,312 --> 00:26:55,649
You had no right to reveal
its existence at all.

461
00:26:55,816 --> 00:26:57,526
Lisbon is my partner.

462
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:07,160
Allegiances, loyalties...
Yes, of course. I...

463
00:27:07,285 --> 00:27:09,746
What was I... thinking?

464
00:27:12,749 --> 00:27:16,545
I understand. You and Lisbon,
you are trusted friends.

465
00:27:18,088 --> 00:27:21,174
You do what you will
Mr. Jane.

466
00:27:22,884 --> 00:27:24,845
That's what you'll do anyway.

467
00:27:24,970 --> 00:27:27,514
J.J., come on.
Don't be like that.

468
00:27:34,521 --> 00:27:37,107
If we're gonna catch Shettrick,
we need to move now.

469
00:27:37,232 --> 00:27:39,651
All we have is Shettrick's
name on a masthead.

470
00:27:39,818 --> 00:27:42,362
- I don't want to rush to judgment.
- Well, nobody rushed.

471
00:27:42,487 --> 00:27:44,656
We took our time to judgment.

472
00:27:44,781 --> 00:27:47,200
But now we're here,
and we need to act.

473
00:27:48,702 --> 00:27:51,788
Hey, if we don't arrest her by tonight
she is going to expose LaRoche.

474
00:27:51,997 --> 00:27:55,083
- Expose him for what?
- I couldn't tell you.

475
00:27:55,792 --> 00:27:59,254
Have you ever thought that maybe
LaRoche's secret should be known?

476
00:27:59,421 --> 00:28:02,174
Endlessly.
But I have come to the conclusion

477
00:28:02,299 --> 00:28:06,052
that whatever happened,
he has punished himself enough.

478
00:28:06,178 --> 00:28:10,765
- I still don't know about Shettrick.
- Yes, you do. In your gut, you know.

479
00:28:11,391 --> 00:28:14,227
She sold you out to Volker.
You know that.

480
00:28:14,352 --> 00:28:17,898
Her actions almost led
to the murder of an 8-year-old boy.

481
00:28:19,024 --> 00:28:21,610
For once in your life, Lisbon,
don't be the voice of reason.

482
00:28:21,735 --> 00:28:23,570
Be the voice of wrath.

483
00:28:25,030 --> 00:28:28,408
All right.
How do we get the bitch?

484
00:28:34,289 --> 00:28:36,374
Sorry, excuse me.
Uh, big to-do in the bullpen.

485
00:28:36,499 --> 00:28:38,293
Lisbon needs help
handling the press.

486
00:28:38,418 --> 00:28:40,629
What's the press doing...
oh, Jane!

487
00:28:41,630 --> 00:28:42,672
Stop!

488
00:28:43,715 --> 00:28:44,799
Tell me what's going on.

489
00:28:44,966 --> 00:28:47,177
Uh, you remember
the drug lord that got away?

490
00:28:47,302 --> 00:28:49,888
- Miguel Leyva.
- Well, CBI found his secret estate.

491
00:28:50,180 --> 00:28:53,308
According to intel, he's sitting poolside
right now with a frisky blonde,

492
00:28:53,433 --> 00:28:56,019
meatball sub
and a fresh shipment of drugs.

493
00:28:56,144 --> 00:28:58,063
- What intel?
- Oh, I don't know.

494
00:28:58,188 --> 00:29:00,815
But the Rapid Response Team
is about to conduct a raid

495
00:29:00,941 --> 00:29:03,735
and that TV reporter
is getting in the way.

496
00:29:03,860 --> 00:29:05,570
- What TV reporter?
- The one from today.

497
00:29:06,154 --> 00:29:08,823
Lisbon invited him
to ride along on the bust.

498
00:29:08,949 --> 00:29:10,867
For God sake, why?

499
00:29:10,992 --> 00:29:13,870
Well... good P.R.
for the Bureau, I don't know.

500
00:29:13,995 --> 00:29:15,830
I guess that's what
she thought you wanted.

501
00:29:17,457 --> 00:29:18,750
Well, I...

502
00:29:23,004 --> 00:29:25,340
Look, we can't let Leyva get away
this time.

503
00:29:25,465 --> 00:29:27,676
We'll stack up on the forward door
with cover on all the windows.

504
00:29:27,801 --> 00:29:30,637
I want a dynamic entry,
shock lock breach, bang and clear.

505
00:29:30,762 --> 00:29:32,472
Guys, she's here.
It's time to start moving

506
00:29:32,597 --> 00:29:34,432
- Let's roll.
- Let's not.

507
00:29:34,557 --> 00:29:36,393
Turn the camera off.
This hasn't been cleared.

508
00:29:36,518 --> 00:29:40,480
Yes, it has. I just left Bertram's office
and he says it's a win-win.

509
00:29:40,605 --> 00:29:42,691
He just wants you to shepherd
our TV colleagues here.

510
00:29:42,816 --> 00:29:45,110
No wonder you didn't want me
asking about Miguel Leyva.

511
00:29:45,235 --> 00:29:46,945
You knew all along
a raid was in the works.

512
00:29:47,070 --> 00:29:48,697
Well, of course.

513
00:29:48,822 --> 00:29:51,157
Okay, just let me make
a phone call before we go.

514
00:29:51,283 --> 00:29:53,076
We don't have time.
You're holding us up. Let's go.

515
00:29:53,201 --> 00:29:55,829
Here's your vest. If you hurry,
you can make the 6:00 news.

516
00:29:57,205 --> 00:29:58,915
Point the camera away from me.

517
00:29:59,207 --> 00:30:01,960
Buh-bye!
Bring back a drug lord!

518
00:30:12,869 --> 00:30:14,204
"This is a high-risk operation."

519
00:30:14,329 --> 00:30:16,247
Surprise, speed,
and domination are key.

520
00:30:16,372 --> 00:30:19,709
Our goals are to clear any threats and
prevent the destruction of any evidence.

521
00:30:20,793 --> 00:30:22,420
Excuse me, what are you doing?

522
00:30:23,421 --> 00:30:25,673
I told you I need
to cancel an appointment.

523
00:30:25,798 --> 00:30:27,842
There's no outside communications
during an operation.

524
00:30:27,967 --> 00:30:29,385
It's standard procedure.

525
00:30:31,221 --> 00:30:32,764
Great.

526
00:30:39,646 --> 00:30:41,189
Moving out.
Remember the tactical plan.

527
00:30:41,314 --> 00:30:42,899
You three stay with Karl.

528
00:30:47,779 --> 00:30:49,239
You want us with?

529
00:30:49,364 --> 00:30:52,408
- Shouldn't we wait in the van?
- Bertram approved full access.

530
00:30:52,533 --> 00:30:54,077
This is great, Brenda.
You're the best.

531
00:30:54,702 --> 00:30:56,371
Stay focused on the breach team.

532
00:31:06,397 --> 00:31:08,149
- Wait!
- Shh! Quiet!

533
00:31:08,274 --> 00:31:10,485
I left my Kevlar vest in the van.

534
00:31:10,610 --> 00:31:12,487
Then you hold right here.
We can't wait for you.

535
00:31:22,747 --> 00:31:25,792
Okay. Okay, okay, okay.

536
00:31:28,836 --> 00:31:30,797
Come on.
Come on, come on.

537
00:31:32,173 --> 00:31:33,216
"Yeah. What up?"

538
00:31:33,341 --> 00:31:34,884
Miguel, it's Brenda Shettrick.
Don't talk. Listen.

539
00:31:35,009 --> 00:31:36,302
They're about to break down
your door.

540
00:31:36,427 --> 00:31:38,763
Now, I will make it go away just
like I did with the last raid.

541
00:31:38,888 --> 00:31:40,932
Just don't say anything
to them.

542
00:31:41,057 --> 00:31:42,517
"Slow down, woman.
What are you talking about?"

543
00:31:42,642 --> 00:31:44,477
No time. Here they come.

544
00:31:52,610 --> 00:31:55,154
Police! Search warrant!
Stand away from the door!

545
00:32:18,970 --> 00:32:22,056
- Is it clear?!
- "Yeah, we're clear."

546
00:32:43,703 --> 00:32:44,745
Hey.

547
00:32:45,913 --> 00:32:48,833
"What's going on?
Get that away from me."

548
00:32:51,294 --> 00:32:55,381
What are you doing here?
Where's Miguel Leyva?

549
00:32:55,548 --> 00:32:58,217
Well, probably relaxing at his pad
wherever the hell that is.

550
00:32:58,342 --> 00:32:59,385
Oh, this place is on the market

551
00:32:59,510 --> 00:33:02,054
but you're gonna need to save
your pennies to post bail.

552
00:33:02,555 --> 00:33:04,640
You're welcome to join us, Brenda.

553
00:33:04,765 --> 00:33:07,643
- We were just reviewing the footage.
- What footage?

554
00:33:08,352 --> 00:33:10,855
Very telegenic.
Don't you think?

555
00:33:11,022 --> 00:33:12,899
"Don't talk. Listen. They're about
to break down your door."

556
00:33:13,065 --> 00:33:15,109
"I will make it go away just
like I did with the last raid."

557
00:33:15,234 --> 00:33:17,320
"Just don't say anything
to them."

558
00:33:17,487 --> 00:33:20,490
You promised me an exclusive.
You weren't kidding.

559
00:33:20,615 --> 00:33:23,576
How much did Miguel Leyva pay you
to tip him off about the drug raid?

560
00:33:24,076 --> 00:33:26,579
- "Go to hell."
- Excellent.

561
00:33:31,918 --> 00:33:33,711
You know how this works, Brenda.

562
00:33:33,878 --> 00:33:36,881
- It'll go a lot easier if you just...
- I do know how this works.

563
00:33:37,423 --> 00:33:40,009
That's what you tell the sheep
on their way to slaughter.

564
00:33:40,968 --> 00:33:42,011
Why do they bleat?

565
00:33:42,136 --> 00:33:44,430
I never understood that when
I watched your interrogations.

566
00:33:46,015 --> 00:33:48,935
- I want a lawyer.
- Well, I guess she's too smart.

567
00:33:49,060 --> 00:33:53,773
Not that smart. We have her
on tape tipping off a cartel boss.

568
00:33:53,898 --> 00:33:56,984
Same way she tipped off Tommy Volker.
She's going down.

569
00:33:57,151 --> 00:34:00,613
- I just wish I knew why.
- Well, I don't think she's gonna tell you.

570
00:34:01,155 --> 00:34:02,323
But I will.

571
00:34:02,448 --> 00:34:05,076
You don't know
the first thing about me.

572
00:34:06,869 --> 00:34:10,998
You were an East Coast prep girl.
College? Uh, Barnard.

573
00:34:11,165 --> 00:34:14,168
Or maybe Mount Holyoke

574
00:34:14,293 --> 00:34:17,171
- for the horseback riding trails.
- She does like horses.

575
00:34:17,296 --> 00:34:18,673
You were a romantic.

576
00:34:19,090 --> 00:34:21,592
You moved to the state capital
because you wanted to expose

577
00:34:21,842 --> 00:34:27,098
fakes and frauds and fall in love,
and write stories in coffee shops.

578
00:34:27,223 --> 00:34:29,684
- She does like coffee.
- A lot of people like coffee.

579
00:34:29,809 --> 00:34:33,187
Here's the one problem...
you couldn't write.

580
00:34:33,312 --> 00:34:35,940
Your skill set was more
managing editor.

581
00:34:36,065 --> 00:34:39,610
Managing editors are the second
highest ranking position at a newspaper.

582
00:34:39,735 --> 00:34:42,238
Yes. The allure of power.

583
00:34:42,530 --> 00:34:43,864
It's why you joined the CBI

584
00:34:43,990 --> 00:34:47,410
so you could rub elbows
with all the big players in town.

585
00:34:47,827 --> 00:34:49,161
You're so off.

586
00:34:50,413 --> 00:34:53,958
Never did fall in love.
Well, at least, uh...

587
00:34:55,126 --> 00:34:57,420
No one fell in love with you.

588
00:34:57,587 --> 00:35:00,590
So you found your thrills
in the arms of power

589
00:35:01,132 --> 00:35:04,343
trading favors
and inside information

590
00:35:05,219 --> 00:35:07,138
to anyone who'd have you.

591
00:35:08,472 --> 00:35:12,685
And in the end, you became
exactly what you hated.

592
00:35:13,644 --> 00:35:17,815
Just another political phony
on the take.

593
00:35:29,619 --> 00:35:31,829
Van Pelt and I made a bet
what's in the plastic ware.

594
00:35:31,954 --> 00:35:34,540
Animal, a vegetable, or mineral.
What do you think?

595
00:35:35,124 --> 00:35:36,667
Check the file cabinet.

596
00:35:38,169 --> 00:35:41,547
Van Pelt says animal.
I say vegetable.

597
00:35:42,048 --> 00:35:44,592
- Van Pelt wins.
- No way!

598
00:35:44,759 --> 00:35:46,469
If it was biological,
you'd freeze it.

599
00:35:46,594 --> 00:35:49,388
Tupperware, it's for food storage.
Has to be vegetable.

600
00:35:50,097 --> 00:35:52,808
- Like what, broccoli?
- I don't know.

601
00:35:56,646 --> 00:35:58,147
Hey, hey, hey.

602
00:35:59,065 --> 00:36:00,441
Check it out.

603
00:36:03,235 --> 00:36:04,487
It exists.

604
00:36:04,654 --> 00:36:05,780
Yeah, it's a box.
Let's go.

605
00:36:06,155 --> 00:36:08,449
Hang on. Don't you care
what's inside?

606
00:36:08,574 --> 00:36:09,784
No.

607
00:36:11,577 --> 00:36:13,454
I think there's something
stuck to the bottom.

608
00:36:15,790 --> 00:36:19,710
- Is that yours to open?
- I was just gonna sneak a peek.

609
00:36:51,242 --> 00:36:55,830
- Thank you for keeping my secret.
- Eh. It was easy.

610
00:36:56,580 --> 00:37:00,251
I'm afraid Brenda Shettrick can still bring
me down with what she knows.

611
00:37:00,376 --> 00:37:03,337
- She won't.
- How can you be sure?

612
00:37:04,088 --> 00:37:05,423
Shettrick likes to trade.

613
00:37:05,548 --> 00:37:08,634
She's cutting a deal with the D.A.
right now to give up her drug lord.

614
00:37:08,759 --> 00:37:10,720
She told Lisbon she'd
forget about Tupperware

615
00:37:10,886 --> 00:37:13,139
if we forget about
blackmail charges.

616
00:37:16,267 --> 00:37:18,728
How did Shettrick know about
the box to begin with?

617
00:37:18,853 --> 00:37:21,063
Only you and I knew
of its existence.

618
00:37:21,188 --> 00:37:24,275
You... and I...
and...

619
00:37:25,693 --> 00:37:27,528
Donny Culpepper.

620
00:37:28,487 --> 00:37:31,490
Small-time thief I hired
to break into your safe.

621
00:37:32,158 --> 00:37:34,452
She must have bought
the information from him.

622
00:37:38,122 --> 00:37:39,749
Well...

623
00:37:42,042 --> 00:37:45,463
This concludes our business
together, Mr. Jane.

624
00:37:45,588 --> 00:37:47,256
I certainly hope not.

625
00:37:50,009 --> 00:37:54,513
You've never asked me why I keep this.
I appreciate that.

626
00:37:54,889 --> 00:37:59,226
- But I suppose you must wonder.
- I wouldn't be human if I didn't.

627
00:38:00,561 --> 00:38:02,980
I hold on to this box
as a warning.

628
00:38:05,232 --> 00:38:09,111
It reminds me of the depths to which
a man can sink if he lets himself.

629
00:38:11,071 --> 00:38:12,531
And...

630
00:38:12,740 --> 00:38:14,658
It reminds me of my mother.

631
00:38:25,044 --> 00:38:28,255
- Good night, J.J.
- Good night, Patrick.

632
00:38:34,470 --> 00:38:37,515
So? Did you look in the box?

633
00:38:38,766 --> 00:38:41,811
- And violate the man's privacy?
- Yes.

634
00:38:41,936 --> 00:38:44,897
What's inside the box is of
far less significance to me

635
00:38:45,022 --> 00:38:46,607
than what the box represents.

636
00:38:46,732 --> 00:38:49,652
I just want to know why you bent over
backwards for that man.

637
00:38:54,990 --> 00:38:56,408
What's important to know

638
00:38:56,534 --> 00:38:59,286
is that a man will go
to extreme lengths to find peace.

639
00:38:59,954 --> 00:39:04,291
- As I must do now.
- What are you talking about?

640
00:39:04,458 --> 00:39:08,003
Until I come out of this room,
I need to be alone, Lisbon.

641
00:39:08,128 --> 00:39:09,588
Alone. No interruptions.

642
00:39:09,713 --> 00:39:11,423
- But...
- No distractions.

643
00:39:12,216 --> 00:39:15,386
- Please.
- Okay.

644
00:39:15,719 --> 00:39:17,847
- Do what you have to do.
- Thank you.

645
00:39:26,730 --> 00:39:29,775
- Hey. Is Jane up there?
- Yeah, but he's busy. What's up?

646
00:39:29,900 --> 00:39:31,277
He asked me to tell him
when I found

647
00:39:31,402 --> 00:39:33,404
the ex-con who assaulted
LaRoche's mother.

648
00:39:33,737 --> 00:39:35,531
Oh, no need. It's over now.

649
00:39:36,365 --> 00:39:37,741
You want to hear
something creepy, though?

650
00:39:37,867 --> 00:39:39,451
The rapist lives with his mom.

651
00:39:40,494 --> 00:39:43,539
- Uh, can I get that address?
- Sure.

652
00:39:50,337 --> 00:39:54,842
Mrs. Saynay, one of my colleagues
called you earlier. I'm with the CBI.

653
00:39:56,844 --> 00:40:01,056
- You can call me Judith.
- I'm Teresa Lisbon.

654
00:40:02,933 --> 00:40:08,606
You people, need my son's help
to help you solve a case?

655
00:40:08,814 --> 00:40:10,232
Is that right?

656
00:40:10,357 --> 00:40:12,443
To help solve a mystery,
at least.

657
00:40:13,694 --> 00:40:18,824
Scott! Get down here!
You got a visitor!

658
00:40:20,367 --> 00:40:24,622
He needs a little
extra motivation sometimes.

659
00:40:24,788 --> 00:40:26,415
How long has your son
lived with you?

660
00:40:28,083 --> 00:40:30,377
Came straight out of jail.

661
00:40:31,295 --> 00:40:33,339
I'd pretend to be flattered...

662
00:40:35,049 --> 00:40:37,843
Uh, but I'm all that he's got.

663
00:40:39,511 --> 00:40:41,472
Vice versa, too.

664
00:40:56,528 --> 00:40:58,989
Hello. I'm Agent Lisbon
with the CBI.

665
00:40:59,156 --> 00:41:01,241
I need you to answer
some questions for me.

666
00:41:04,620 --> 00:41:06,121
You mean you...you...

667
00:41:06,246 --> 00:41:09,249
- You don't know?
- What?

668
00:41:10,834 --> 00:41:14,713
Scott hasn't...
spoken in nine years.

669
00:41:17,257 --> 00:41:18,300
Well, why?

670
00:41:18,425 --> 00:41:23,263
Well, the... the day before his trial
somebody broke into his apartment

671
00:41:23,389 --> 00:41:25,057
while he was sleeping, and...

672
00:41:26,141 --> 00:41:30,521
they injected him with a sedative
and cut out his tongue.

673
00:41:31,021 --> 00:41:35,734
The police, they never figured out
who did it you know, or why, or...

674
00:41:38,862 --> 00:41:41,573
And they never found
his tongue.

